eral shapes never silent\\\" line was corrected: constructor non-literals are fault conduits by design, not obligations.\\n- CENSUS-FLOOR REASONING: the floor catches a silently truncated scan (empty, single-file, or short derivation fails even when every surviving arm is witnessed); the reverse witness check catches a deleted or narrowed production branch by orphaning its witness. Raising is routine with new refusals; lowering requires saying why.\\n- DEFECT (caught by the new tests, fixed before review): the first `DecodeQuiesceProof` draft omitted both open counts from the safe-rule disjunction — `safe:true` with `open_child_count:1` validated. The per-conjunct safe-lie fixtures (one violated fact each) caught it; counts now return through `checkQuiesceCounts` into the rule.\\n- COMPLEMENTS, NOT SAMPLES: 6 providers × 2 profiles swept; 4 statuses\\n[tool output bounded: strategy=head, original_bytes=41021, visible_bytes=40000]\\n<system-reminder>\\nFull output saved to: /Users/iv/.local/share/muse/sessions/2026/09/06/01a077c8-d88a-7931-843c-3e9dddbe9444/tool-outputs/df579dc2-f940-4282-bba2-b37f8debddc2/call_01a077c903fc7241a799523c2957f4a8-bash.txt\\nFull output is longer than the visible window.\\nUse bash tools like head, tail, cat, sed, or grep to inspect and search the full output.\\n</system-reminder>\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 41021,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 10256,\n  \"truncated\": true\n}"}}}
