alk surrogate semantics, rune measure, env-id/SemVer/arch grammars, exact six-member Tuple, §10.8.1 Environment Observation reusing the tuple model. Battery: census, frame/measure/tuple/identity agreement, observation. Frozen `sessadapter`/`dirnode` production untouched. Commit afdba1d (signed), PR #35 published.\\n- FINDING: sessadapter+dirnode raw-scan surrogate gates REFUSE wire bodies carrying literal backslash-u text (`cursor` value `\\\\ud800` text) while environ+provhost+canonicaljson string-walk gates ACCEPT — proven via DecodeTuple/CheckScanRequest/Canonicalize. sessadapter `TestSurrogateGateAgreesWithCanonicalJSON` is one-directional (`!localRefuses && sharedRefuses`) and hides exactly this class. Ledgered in frame_agreement_test.go; unifying the frozen scanners is the recorded follow-up.\\n- FINDING: truncated/malformed escapes refuse at the surrogate arm (raw scan) vs the syntax arm (string walk); wrong identity schema/version refuses at the member arm (provhost) vs the dispatch registry (canonicaljson). Same verdicts, different arms — ledgered per-judge, not papered over.\\n- FINDING: battery caught its author's parity error — run-3 backslashes (`\\\\\\\\\\\\ud800`) are a real lone escape (odd runs escape, even runs quote), not divergence; row corrected to all-refuse before green.\\n- EVIDENCE: attached TASK-260830-3bkz0c_boundary.md (7/7 AC rows with call sites) + TASK-260830-3bkz0c_mutation-log.md. Narrowing mutants 6/6 killed (N1/N2/N3/N4/N6 + token-preserving T1 raw-scan rewrite with census still green); D1 delete-only killed, scored as existence only. Tree sha-verified identical post-battery.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (19 pkgs), environ `-race` exit 0, cover 76.1%, `go vet ./...` + `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (unchanged), catalog generate no-diff, `go build ./...` exit 0.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off with CR published (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 1035 — Directory-node leaf round-2 rework: rev1 B1/B2/B3 closed, 185-mutant battery\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-ljkj8r round-2 rework (review-verdict-rev1, changes requested, B1–B3 blocking). Test-only additions inside `internal/dirnode/` (`bound_census_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `query_operations_test.go`, `arm_identity_test.go`) plus four one-line fixture-surgery fixes (`query_test.go` unknown_field + missing caller, `manifest_test.go` missing member, `probe_test.go` missing member) and three edge extensions (findings 4097, cursor 1/1024 admission, projection bound edges). No production behavior change. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (B1): bound census ported from the sessadapter leaf — 101 production-derived sites (9 helpers + len/length-var guards, 10-shape space with 6 derived + 4 stated), 72 driven + 29 exempt mechanism/plumbing. Edge drivers prove min-1/min/max/max+1 through the production entry. Battery: 185 applied / 142 behavioural kills / 43 equivalent-with-bound / 0 survivors, zero not-applied, zero compile failures. Census-only kills scored separately (2 live census mutants + 3 synthetic gate proofs).\\n- FIX (B2): `TestDecodeQueryAllOperationsAdmit` drives 17/17 registry operations (was 5/17); 40+ validator defects through DecodeQuery including the review probes environments/\\\"root\\\", jobs/\\\"pwned\\\", distinct/\\\"secret\\\" (battery V01–V03, all killed). Zero functions at 0.0% (was 10, all §10.8.5 validators).\\n- FIX (B3): unknown_field rebuilt without the duplicate member + reachability proof; audit found the same rename-instead-of-delete slide in three more missing vectors, all fixed to deletions + message-identity proof. Protocol relabeled-major placeholder verified genuine (overridden with a real relabeled frame).\\n- FINDINGS: (1) Closed vocabularies mask bound narrowings — 11 count ceilings equal their vocabulary size (no ceiling+1 member buildable) and 20 element bounds cannot discriminate behind the outer gate; all recorded as equivalents, never survivors. (2) Count/index gates coincide at the 65th operation — each single weakening is masked behind the other; pinned jointly. (3) Test scaffolds must not size probes from production constants: the frame suite initially referenced MaxFrameBytes and went green under a widened constant; now retyped (frameBoundBytes) like all fixtures. Same fix applied to two protocol oversize vectors and the uint53 ceiling probe.\\n- EVIDENCE: attached TASK-260830-ljkj8r_round2.md (verdicts, equivalence classes, full 185-row table, 9/9 AC mapping). Production files byte-identical (battery is copy-back per mutant; post-run grep for mutant literals clean).\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (18 pkgs), `-race` on dirnode exit 0, `go vet ./...` and `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=94, unchanged). Dirnode cover 74.9% → 83.3%.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n### 0930 — Directory-node leaf: `internal/dirnode` implemented with enumerated census first\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-ljkj8r (second leaf of STORY-260830-3drr2m). New package `internal/dirnode`: two-major manifest bootstrap, envelope framing, manifest/probe/scan/Directory-Query framing, façade host checks, Structured Error 1.2.0 refusals. Six traceability rows (88 → 94), README paragraph. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- CENSUS FIRST: the leaf-1 lesson (seven rounds, one repeating mistake class) is applied before the battery, not after. `census_test.go` enumerates 10 of 10 AST shapes carrying an error construction (literal, binary-expr with rendered key, constructor registration, New-outside-body, New-as-value, ctor alias in every position, closure-hidden call, aliased import, frameFault literal) with synthetic proofs and named residue. Result: 147 derived arms (145 witnessed + 2 defensive), 8 constructors. The census caught 5 missing witness rows and 3 vacuous fixture vectors during authoring.\\n- NO-OP-PROOF VECTORS: every fixture-surgery site uses `replaceOnce`, which fails when the needle is absent — a mutation that changes nothing can no longer pass against a still-valid body.\\n- FINDINGS: (1) §10.8.5 prose names `query_cursor_mismatch` but the pinned error registry does not register it — cursor reuse refuses as `query_invalid` with a cursor-mismatch detail. (2) The response envelope carries its own `schema` + `schema_version` (1.0.0 both majors): the downgrade tuple names a response schema_version no schemaless reading can carry. (3) `node manifest is not canonical JSON` is reachable, not defensive: extensions values cross opaquely while the canonicalizer enforces depth 256 (300-deep vector proves it). (4) `failCapability` removed — no entry point in this deliverable raises `capability_unavailable`; the taxonomy test pins the 8 emitted codes instead of keeping a dead constructor for census symmetry.\\n- EVIDENCE: narrowing-mutant battery M1–M8, all killed, 0 survivors (M1 downgrade-retryable, M2 v1-macos, M3 conditional-upgrade, M4 scan-replay, M5 index-contiguity, M6 relabeled-schema-version, M7 reasonless-capability, M8 aliased-import with full behavioral suite green). Every mutant copy-aside/copy-back with `cmp` clean; exit codes unpiped. Census-only kills (M8's 4) scored separately.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (18 pkgs), `-count=3` and `-race` on dirnode exit 0, `-race` on traceability+tracecheck exit 0, `go vet ./...` and `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=94). Full-repo `-race` not run (exceeds one bounded call; raced every touched package instead). Dirnode cover 75.0%.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n### 0618 — Session-adapter leaf round-4 rework: rev3 B4/B5/B6 closed as classes, N6 fixed in code\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2z3se0 round-4 rework (review-verdict-rev3, changes requested, B4–B6 blocking + N6). Test-only additions inside `internal/sessadapter/` (`zero_absent_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `import_census_test.go`) plus a two-line production-test fix in `inventory_test.go` and this entry. No production behavior change; the 323-arm inventory floor is untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (B4): the zero/absent-fact class is now derived, not listed. `TestEnvelopeEchoEmptyStringRefuses` iterates the echo members from the production Required slices (request [:2], success/failure [:4] = 10 rows) with wants from `ProtocolID`/`ProtocolVersion`/`wantRequest()`, each driven as `\\\"\\\"` through its entry point; `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesAbsentAdapterRefuses` deletes each required adapter name (set derived from `DoctorRequiredCapabilities`) and both writers together; `TestCapabilityUsableAbsentIsNotUsable` deletes every `capabilityOrder` name through both `CapabilityUsable` and `capabilityMapUsable`; `TestCheckDoctorHealthyRefusesEmptyRequiredName` pins the name gate against `\\\"\\\"`.\\n- FIX (B5): `TestStringBoundEdges` (17 rows: all 16 survivor `checkStringBounds` maxima plus probe detail 0..2048) drives min-1/min/max/max+1 through the entry; `TestArrayBoundEdges` drives 0/1/max/max+1 for argv count, disposition lists, contract rows, and versions. Same-width sortable fixtures where the gate orders members (zero-padded `c01..c64` contract ids, `1.0.0-a01..a33` prerelease versions); the 8-entry disposition refusal lands on the count arm because it fires before the element gates.\\n- FIX (B6): new `TestAxerrorImportsAreUnaliased` — every production import of the error path must bind `axerror` (default or identical alias); renamed, blank, and dot bindings fail, with a zero-importer fail-closed guard. The constructor census is now sound as written without special-casing aliases. Synthetic alias vectors prove the gate shape.\\n- FIX (N6): `constructorSitesInFile` now reports the function-local registered-name case (`case !topLevel`, was a silent fall-through), matching its comment; pinned by synthetic `TestConstructorSitesReportFunctionLocalRegisteredName` (reports locally, stays exempt at package level).\\n- EVIDENCE: narrowing-mutant battery 36/36 killed, 0 survived — exactly the reviewer's 35 survivors (10 envelope + 3 presence + 20 bounds + 2 alias) plus the N6 arm. Every mutant grep-confirmed present and `go vet`-clean before its verdict; tree sha-verified identical after. A3/A4 additionally hold the constructor census green, so the kill comes from the import census, not the floor. Harness lesson: piped `go test | tail` reports tail's exit 0 — the first battery run showed 0/36 for that reason; all gate statuses here are unpiped direct exit codes.\\n- GATES: `go build ./...` 0, `go vet ./...` 0, `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./...` 17/17 exit 0 (sessadapter 976 PASS/0 FAIL, cover 81.5%), `-race` on sessadapter exit 0, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=88, unchanged — no behavior change, no new AC rows).\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n### 0515 — Session-adapter leaf round-3 rework: rev2 B1–B3 closed, N4/N5 closed-or-bounded\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2z3se0 round-3 rework (review-verdict-rev2, changes requested, B1–B3 blocking + N4/N5). All changes inside `internal/sessadapter/` except this entry. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (B1): `checkValidateResult` no longer calls `checkValidateNullability` — the pinned §7.8 validate success member list names no target members, so the request-body nullability rule cannot apply to successes. Archive-mode validate success now passes through `CheckSuccessBody`; `TestValidateSuccessAdmitsEveryMode` drives staged/live/archive successes. The round-2 anomaly below is resolved, not decided: the document's own success-body list settles it.\\n- FIX (B2): `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec` now compares the Members gate map as a set against the derived list for all four tail bodies (success, failure, manifest, doctor); the `manifestMembers` local is renamed `derivedManifest` so it cannot shadow the production map; the log reports member-map comparisons (20 across 21 bodies; SupportedContractVersions has no production gate map by design).\\n- FIX (B3): new `TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction` derives the constructor denominator from production — every `axerror.New` site must sit inside a registered constructor body, and the registered set must equal the error-constructing vars exactly. The inventory header sentence now states what both gates do.\\n- FIX (N4): new `TestCheckCallBindingZeroFactsRefuse` — all five `CheckCallBinding` zero-fact exemptions refuse through their own arms.\\n- FIX (N5): `vocabularyTablesInFile` handles shared and paired multi-name initializers (synthetic vectors added); the tagless-switch exemption is confined to `readUTF16Escape` by function name (`classifySwitch` + `TestSwitchClassifierNamesItsExemption`); the census stated bound now names the function-local obligation lists (pinned behaviourally, both directions) and the const/regexp shapes (absent from production).\\n- EVIDENCE: narrowing-mutant battery over the rework scope, every mutant grep-confirmed present and compiling before its verdict; full gates green (see the attached rework-evidence note).\\n\\n### 0444 — Session-adapter leaf rework: all four blocking verdict findings closed, one anomaly reported\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2z3se0 round-2 rework (review-verdict-rev1, changes requested, F1–F4 blocking + F5–F7). All changes inside `internal/sessadapter/`; previously reviewed files untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (F1): nine inline closed unions → table loops with `valid*` consultants (mode, direction, entry status, registry-entry status, evidence result, candidate kind, role, context-free ops). Refusal details byte-identical, 323-arm inventory unchanged. Census scanner extended two ways: named slice/map types resolve package-wide; new `TestNoUnregisteredInlineVocabularies` forbids any chain comparing one operand against 2+ closed values. The new detector immediately found two more real unions (probe candidate kind, manifest/probe context dispatch) the reviewer had not listed. Spec pins for all eight unions; registrations 55 → 63.\\n- FIX (F2): `collectFileArms` exempts only the definition Name in its ValueSpec; `var x = ctor` fails package-level and function-local. `TestConstructorAliasSpellingsFailDerivation` replays all four probes on synthetic sources.\\n- FIX (F3): `TestSurrogatePairSweep` — every high × {lowLo−1, lowLo, lowHi, lowHi+1} plus full-range interior for three highs, verdicts from test-local literals: 2058 refused + 5124 admitted.\\n- FIX (F4): per-member drivers for doctor-required (4×2 writer variants), nullability (4×2 branches, request side), applicable checks (3) + nullable-bool types (3).\\n- FIX (F5/F6/F7): same-length echo forgery; exact/over frame edges on all three envelopes; four zero-value host-fact refusals.\\n- EVIDENCE: narrowing-mutant battery 26 killed + 1 control-green / 27 measured, every mutant grep-confirmed present and compiling before its verdict (`/tmp/mutant-battery.py`, log attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-battery-rev2.log`). Gates: `go test ./...` 17/17 exit 0, sessadapter 904 PASS/0 FAIL, `-count=3` green, `-race` green, cover 81.1% → 81.4%, vet + GOOS=windows vet exit 0, gofmt clean.\\n- ANOMALY (behavior preserved, needs product decision): `checkValidateNullability` is shared by request and success bodies, but validate success bodies carry no target members and the member set is exact, so archive-mode success ALWAYS refuses (`carries a target member` on absent members, reproduced with a scratch test) while staged/live success passes vacuously — the success-side call is a mode gate in disguise. F4 driven request-side where the rule is well-defined. Options: scope the rule to requests / redesign absent-handling / declare archive success impossible.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n## 2026-09-05\\n\\n### 0935 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-6 rework: switch vocabularies, ExecRunner frame loss, flake bound\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti round-6 verdict (changes requested, two blocking findings F1/F2 plus the nondeterministic suite). Carries the reviewer's findings into the logbook — the reviewer deliberately left LOGBOOK.md out of their delta. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (F1, blocking): the three switch-shaped closed vocabularies the census could not see (envelope member set `checkResponseMembers` ← `DecodeResponse:416`, execution profile `ProfileMapping` ← `DecodeSpawnPlan:100`, transaction state `validStatusState` ← `DecodeStatusOutcome:126`) are package-level maps now (`responseMembers`, `profileNames`, `statusStates`), each consulted by a membership check, so the existing census derives them with no scanner change. Each carries a pinned-document derivation (`TestResponseMembersAreDerivedFromSpec` from the two 7.2 envelope sentences with `ok = true/false` normalized, `TestProfileNamesAreDerivedFromSpec` from the two 7.7 profile sentences with exactly-one-span guards, `TestStatusStatesAreDerivedFromSpec` from the 7.5 ProviderTransactionStatus state span), a census registration (19 → 22 vocabularies, both directions), and a production entry-point refusal row (envelope/`bogus` via DecodeResponse, `ProfileMapping(codex, bogus)`, bogus status state via DecodeStatusOutcome). `TestAllProductionSwitchesAreClassified` pins the residue: every production switch must be a classified dispatch (the one remaining switch dispatches on an already-validated state), so a new switch-shaped gate fails until classified. The \\\"closes the class by construction\\\" header now states the derived shapes plus this guard instead of an unstated-empty residue.\\n- FIX (F2, blocking): `ExecRunner` discarded judgeable results through two races on `Host.Call`'s primary path. (a) `return Result{}, writeErr` before stdout was ever considered: an EPIPE racing the plugin's exit threw away valid correlated frames. (b) Found during this rework by driving `Run` directly (2 of 20 crash-script iters returned `read |0: file already closed`): `Wait` closes `StdoutPipe`/`StderrPipe` read ends after seeing the process exit, racing a drain still in flight — this, not EPIPE, is what misclassified the stdin-draining `exit 3` fixture. Fix per the file's own comments: judge whenever possible (non-empty stdout governs; empty stdout with a known exit classifies the crash through the Result), surface write/close/wait failures only with empty stdout and no known exit, and drain over `os.Pipe` pairs owned by `Run` so no later Close can interrupt a drain. New tests `TestExecRunnerKeepsValidFrameWhenPluginIgnoresStdin` (200 calls, zero discards) and `TestExecRunnerClassifiesCrashExitDeterministically` (50 crash calls, all `plugin exited without a response`): both FAIL on the pre-fix runner (2/200 frames discarded; crash misclassified as `runner reported no result`, each verified by swapping the pre-fix `runner.go` back with sha256-verified restore) and pass post-fix.\\n- FLAKE BOUND: post-fix `go test ./internal/provhost/ -count=1` 30/30 green in two 15-run chunks (pre-fix: 3 red in 50 per the reviewer). The two F2 loops above are the deterministic pins; the old single-shot `TestExecRunnerReportsCrashExit` stays as a third witness.\\n- EVIDENCE: `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `GOOS=windows go vet ./internal/provhost/` exit 0; gofmt clean; `go test ./... -count=1` green (15 packages); provhost `-race` green; provhost cover 86.5% → 86.0% (new judge/pipe branches). Widening mutants re-planted against the new maps (envelope/profile/status `\\\"bogus\\\"`, plus an unclassified-switch plant): each dies three ways — derivation, census subtest, entry-point row — with cp-aside/sha256 restores; the one vacuous-green run in the sequence (a gofmt-realigned anchor that planted nothing) was caught by the grep-plant assertion and re-run with the corrected anchor.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n### 0926 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-6 rework: the vocabulary class closed by census\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti round-5 verdict (changes requested, single blocking finding F1r). Test-only rework: new `internal/provhost/closed_vocabulary_census_test.go`, `requireVocabulary` comparison fix in `closed_vocabularies_test.go`. Production untouched; uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (F1r): the nine membership-checked vocabularies with no derivation (manifest/probe/capability/identity/identify/quiesce/spawn/status member sets plus the yolo mapping) are now derived from the pinned document — example-JSON keys for 7.3/7.4, first-sentence code spans for the capability-value sentence, TableRowAt Field rows for the 5.5 identity table, per-span member declarations for the 7.5 SpawnPlan/SafeBoundaryProof/ProviderTransactionStatus rows, braced-cell parsing for the identify-session success body, per-row provider-plus-first-flag for the 7.7 table. The census parses production source for package-level []string/map[string]bool/map[string]string with membership use (unknownMember argument, map index, range operand) and requires each of the 19 found vocabularies to carry an executing derivation, in both directions.\\n- EVIDENCE: probe_widen.json replay, full-package runs, cp+sha256 restores: W1–W9 KILLED (each red three ways — derivation, census subtest, entry-point refusal row), W10/R2/R4 killed, R1/R3 survive as the stated behaviour-preserving bounds. Fail-closed attacks all red: wrong type name, bad cell marker, off-table identity window, unregistered planted vocabulary (`has no registered spec derivation`), blinded string-map scan (`names no production vocabulary`), dropped registration. `requireVocabulary` now uses reflect.DeepEqual, so the V4 joined-member mutant is killed by the derivation alone. Gates: build/vet/GOOS=windows vet exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./...` 15/15 green, provhost -race green, provhost cover 86.5% unchanged. CORRECTION (round-6 review): the \\\"15/15 green\\\" was one observation of a nondeterministic suite, not a property — the clean tree failed `go test ./internal/provhost/` 3 times in 50 runs under load (F2 below). Green-suite claims now carry a run count.\\n- ANOMALY: the capability-value sentence shares its window with the warnings sentence, so a naive span read derives five members including warnings; the derivation truncates to the declaring sentence. The bare 5.5 closed sentence repeats in four sections, so the identity quote carries its schema opener to stay unique. The *Required order lists are excluded from the census by construction (missingMember-only use), which is what keeps R1/R3 surviving.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n### 0830 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-5 rework: the 28 real survivors, closed by derivation\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti round-4 verdict (changes requested, 106 mutants, 76 killed, 30 survived, 2 stated bounds, 28 real). Test-only rework in `internal/provhost` plus one comment restatement; production untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (F1, blocking): the eight closed vocabularies the three existing specdoc derivations did not cover are now derived the same way in `internal/provhost/closed_vocabularies_test.go` — probe statuses and evidence from the Section 7.4 sentences, architectures from 7.4 prose cross-checked against the 7.5 probe request row, probe platforms from that row (sorted both sides: the row lists macos first, the implementation holds sorted order), quiesce blockers from the 7.5 enum sentence, identity kinds from the 5.5 table row, identify confidence and matched-evidence from the 7.5 identify-session row. Each widening mutant from the verdict battery (partial, assumed, 386, freebsd, other, legacy_alias, guess, guessed) is killed twice: once by the derivation equality, once by an exact-member refusal row through the production entry point.\\n- FIX (F2): last-element substitution rows for both manifest order loops, first-element-unknown platform row (aix, still sorted-unique so it reaches the vocab check), and first/last missing-registry-key probe rows.\\n- FIX (F3): NUL-injection fixtures for both SpawnPlan members that reach exec — argv element and env-literal value — via JSON `\\\\u0000` escapes.\\n- FIX (F4): identity provider-correlation now pinned with the equal-length claude/gemini pair (both 6), with a length-equality guard so the fixture cannot go blind silently.\\n- FIX (F5): all ten bound+1 rows plus exactness acceptances on both sides (including the first SP8 fixture on either side: 65537 refused, 65536 accepted). LESSON: a bound+1 mutant is killed only by bound+1 exactly — the first SP8 draft totalled 69,632 bytes, above even the widened bound, and survived. Same class as the token-floor finding: the obligation must carry the literal.\\n- FIX (F6): aliasing tests for both copy guarantees (`MutationOperations`, `Capabilities`); the quiesce safe-rule comment restated to name backgroundNull as folded into !background by `rawNullableBool` (unreachable, not untested); the vacuous `runner.spawned() != 0` assertion on a Runner never handed to `RequireCapability` removed and restated as structural.\\n- BONUS: the manifest digit-first provider-id row also kills MA8, which the verdict battery listed as killed but is now pinned at the manifest layer too.\\n- ANOMALY: the first NUL-row draft wrote raw NUL bytes into the Go source (binary file, invalid-JSON refusal instead of the NUL arm); replaced with `\\\\u0000` escapes and verified zero NUL bytes remain. S1's ExecRunner fork/exec flake reappeared in 2 of ~30 full-package mutant runs; every affected mutant also failed its targeted test, so no verdict rests on it.\\n- EVIDENCE: 29-mutant replay (the 28 real survivors plus MA8) with the reviewer's own harness and spec files: 29 killed, 0 survived. `go build`, `go vet`, `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./... -count=1` 15/15 green, provhost `-race` green, provhost cover 86.4% → 86.5%.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n### 0510 — Provider conformance-harness leaf: operation decoders, derived complements, inventory census 60 → 162\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti (final leaf of STORY-260830-3jqsx1). New `internal/provhost` operation layer: manifest (7.3), probe + capability gate (7.4/8.3), profile mapping (7.7), quiescence proof (7.6), SpawnPlan for launch/resume, Provider Identity Record + identify result (5.5), and the single `(operation, operation_id)` key (7.5), with Host.Call conformance sequences (manifest/probe/resume/identify/quiesce end to end, 21 fail-closed capability-by-status tuples with zero processes started, byte-identical lost-prepare retry, changed-body `idempotency_mismatch` passthrough, child-code passthrough table). Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- MECHANISM (leaf-2 item closed here): the derived refusal-arm inventory parses production AST — every `&frameFault` literal, every literal `integrity(...)` argument (with the `decodeStrictObject`-fault wrapper expanded over the derived frame detail set), every `parseMajor` rejection branch keyed by enclosing condition, and every literal first argument to the six refusal constructors — and checks both directions (every derived arm witnessed, every witness derived) plus a census floor. This leaf raised the floor 60 → 162 and added 102 witnesses, one per new arm.\\n- BLIND SHAPES (stated, not fixed): a one-line wrapper fronting a constructor and an aliased constructor at an unexercised site are both invisible to the arm walk and the site audit; both measured empty in this tree and neither shape was introduced. The file header's \\\"non-literal shapes never silent\\\" line was corrected: constructor non-literals are fault conduits by design, not obligations.\\n- CENSUS-FLOOR REASONING: the floor catches a silently truncated scan (empty, single-file, or short derivation fails even when every surviving arm is witnessed); the reverse witness check catches a deleted or narrowed production branch by orphaning its witness. Raising is routine with new refusals; lowering requires saying why.\\n- DEFECT (caught by the new tests, fixed before review): the first `DecodeQuiesceProof` draft omitted both open counts from the safe-rule disjunction — `safe:true` with `open_child_count:1` validated. The per-conjunct safe-lie fixtures (one violated fact each) caught it; counts now return through `checkQuiesceCounts` into the rule.\\n- COMPLEMENTS, NOT SAMPLES: 6 providers × 2 profiles swept; 4 statuses\\n[tool output bounded: strategy=head, original_bytes=41021, visible_bytes=40000]\\n<system-reminder>\\nFull output saved to: /Users/iv/.local/share/muse/sessions/2026/09/06/01a077c8-d88a-7931-843c-3e9dddbe9444/tool-outputs/df579dc2-f940-4282-bba2-b37f8debddc2/call_01a077c903fc7241a799523c2957f4a8-bash.txt\\nFull output is longer than the visible window.\\nUse bash tools like head, tail, cat, sed, or grep to inspect and search the full output.\\n</system-reminder>\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 41021,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 10256,\n  \"truncated\": true\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
