{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c747","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a077c8-d88a-7931-843c-3e9dddbe9444"},"sequence":510,"recorded_at":1780531400001015,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d502244e-0589-4672-9c20-02af4f4b0b68","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d502244e-0589-4672-9c20-02af4f4b0b68","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d502244e-0589-4672-9c20-02af4f4b0b68"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"3508841e-353d-47a7-80d1-56eb83da1ae0"},"task_id":"3508841e-353d-47a7-80d1-56eb83da1ae0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"3508841e-353d-47a7-80d1-56eb83da1ae0","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-17-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -rn \\\"10/10\\\\|skipped=0\\\\|10-row\\\\|recordVerdict.*logs\\\\|SKIP line plus\\\" internal/secconftest/ README.md LOGBOOK.md 2>&1 | head -n 40\\necho \\\"===\\\"\\ncat -n LOGBOOK.md | sed -n '1,35p' 2>&1\",\n  \"description\": \"Sweep superseded numbers and logbook lines\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"LOGBOOK.md:11:- C2: `Report()` reads the live counters; `TestSkipReportReadsRecordedVerdicts` records synthetic verdicts, asserts the report moves, restores state (gutting `recordVerdict` reddens it, battery A4). The round-1 `skipped=0` citation was a constant — genuine datum is 0 `--- SKIP` / 0 `--- FAIL` lines under `go test -v` on darwin non-root, now cited in README/outcome/doc.go.\\nLOGBOOK.md:22:- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest.md` (6/6 AC rows with call sites, 10-row mutant table: 4 narrowing + 4 arm-deletion + 2 census-only, 10/10 killed, 0 survivors; M4 token-preserving mutant with 222-pass/1-fail full-suite run; darwin skip report skipped=0; digest `5569f34caab734eb` x3).\\n===\\n     1\\t# Flight Logbook\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n     4\\t> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\t## 2026-09-06\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\t### 2105 — secconftest round-2 rework: C1–C4 closed, instrument stops reporting untrue things\\n     9\\t- SCOPE: TASK-260830-7a0s2c round-2 (review-verdict-rev1, C1–C4 blocking). Production (test instrument) only in `internal/secconftest`: `crash.go` (finalize gate + `ErrRollbackPastFinalize`, `RemainingArmed`), `skip.go` (`Report()` over live counters, real `mkfifo` fifo probe), `skip_fifo_unix/windows.go` (new, `makeFifo` + fault seam), `hostile.go` untouched, `fuzz_test.go` (no-op poles), `doc.go` (bounds). Leaf-1 `internal/secprim` untouched (`git diff HEAD -- internal/secprim` empty).\\n    10\\t- C1: `Rollback` now refuses post-commit with `ErrRollbackPastFinalize` and leaves committed bytes intact; `TestTransactorRefusesRollbackPastFinalize` commits-then-rolls-back (the arm it is named for) plus both old arms. Deleting the gate is killed by it (battery A1).\\n    11\\t- C2: `Report()` reads the live counters; `TestSkipReportReadsRecordedVerdicts` records synthetic verdicts, asserts the report moves, restores state (gutting `recordVerdict` reddens it, battery A4). The round-1 `skipped=0` citation was a constant — genuine datum is 0 `--- SKIP` / 0 `--- FAIL` lines under `go test -v` on darwin non-root, now cited in README/outcome/doc.go.\\n    12\\t- C3: fifo probe builds a real FIFO (`syscall.Mkfifo`+Lstat; Windows stub unavailable) with a fault seam (`TestSkipFifoProbeAttemptsItsCapability` kills a success-on-failure weakening, battery N14). All 4 probes gate real tests: symlink→escape witness, fifo→byte-exchange fixture, mode-bits+nonroot→denial test (4/4 wired, was 1/4).\\n    13\\t- C4: all 8 listed survivors closed — digest report/name distinguishing tests (N1–N3), bidi rune-for-rune pin + corpus coverage (N4–N5), Gate pin+drive for all 18 classes (N6), verdict counter test (A4), commit-requires-prepare with planted staged file (A3). Battery re-derived from this tree: 29 applied / 0 NOT_APPLIED / 0 COMPILE_FAIL / 0 VET_FAIL, 27 killed (15 narrowing + 8 arm-deletion + 4 census-only), 2 survived with bounds: N16 driver-delegation (read-verified + arrival-counted) and S1 mode-bits-false (survives-as-SKIP by construction — the SKIP line is the signal). N10 token-preserving mutant killed by the full behavioral suite; tree sha256-identical after the battery.\\n    14\\t- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest-round2.md` (6/6 AC rows corrected, 29-row mutant table with bounds, gates with exit codes) + `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_mutant-battery-round2.log` + full-test log.\\n    15\\t- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (21 pkgs), secconftest `-race` exit 0, `./... -cover` exit 0 (secconftest 89.3%, secprim 94.4% unchanged), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet/build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (94 cases, unchanged), 8/8 fuzz `-fuzztime=100x` exit 0 with no corpus written, digest `5569f34caab734eb` x5 processes.\\n    16\\t- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\t### 2035 — secconftest instrument leaf: runners, fake clocks, crash points, fuzz, hostile strings, skips\\n    19\\t- SCOPE: TASK-260830-7a0s2c (second leaf of STORY-260830-1i3qu7). New package `internal/secconftest` (doc/runner/clock/crash/fuzz/hostile/skip + 6 test files): sorted deterministic Runner with execution digest and zero-call refusal, wall-clock-free Fake with Recording wiring detector, CR-MAT-* Injector over a three-phase Transactor with §13.13 outcomes and idempotency_mismatch, 8 Fuzz targets through one shared Driver with seed arrival proofs, 18-class spec-derived hostile roster plus symlink-escape commit witness, 4 probed capabilities with strict-platform failure. Leaf-1 `internal/secprim` production untouched; `task-board.config.json` gains the 8 required fuzz validation commands (pinned by `TestConfiguredValidationRunsEveryFuzzTargetWithFixedBudget`, which failed until registered).\\n    20\\t- FINDING: the repo already forces fuzz registration — a new Fuzz target without a config line fails `TestConfiguredValidationRunsEveryFuzzTargetWithFixedBudget` plus its coverage parent. The instrument therefore cannot silently add unfuzzed-in-CI targets.\\n    21\\t- FINDING (M6): a Fake leaking `time.Now` is caught by two fresh fakes disagreeing (real timestamps in the failure), not just by the sleep test — the stronger kill.\\n    22\\t- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest.md` (6/6 AC rows with call sites, 10-row mutant table: 4 narrowing + 4 arm-deletion + 2 census-only, 10/10 killed, 0 survivors; M4 token-preserving mutant with 222-pass/1-fail full-suite run; darwin skip report skipped=0; digest `5569f34caab734eb` x3).\\n    23\\t- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (21 pkgs), `-race` exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (secconftest 86.9%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (94 cases, unchanged). 8/8 fuzz targets pass 5s smoke and `-fuzztime=100x` with no corpus written.\\n    24\\t- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n    25\\t\\n    26\\t### 1939 — secprim round-3 rework: C1 handle binding, C2 classify-before-close, C3 spelling bound, N24 restored\\n    27\\t- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2ciy0s round-3 (review-verdict-rev2, C1–C4 blocking). Production: `internal/secprim/nofollow.go` (`guardRootMatches` fstat dev/ino compare via `os.SameFile`, new `guard root mismatch` site in `Guard.Open`); `open_member_unix.go` (classify-before-close at both sites); spelling bound stated in `errors.go`/`inventory_test.go`/README + `TestRefusalInventorySpellingBoundIsStated`; honest reparse mapping in both windows files + README. Tests: `guard_root_test.go` (foreign-handle refusal + matched control, cross-platform), depth-3/4 full-string vectors in `open_unix_test.go`.\\n    28\\t- ROOT CAUSE (C1): `openCommitRelative(root, _ string, ...)` discarded `guard.root`; unix walked the handle, Windows the path — one entry, two containment roots. Fixed in shared `Guard.Open` so both answer identically.\\n    29\\t- ROOT CAUSE (C2): from iteration 2 `previous == current`; closing before `classifyCommitErr` fstat'd a recycled fd, misreporting depth>=2 symlink hops as `open failed`. Revert reproduces the exact reported string.\\n    30\\t- FINDING (N24): arm-drop spelling KILLS (`target special file` vs `target directory`); the `Size() > 0` spelling SURVIVES (empty dirs report Size > 0) — rev2 withdrew the wrong spelling. FINDING (D14): scripted shape is COMPILE-FAIL (unused import), superseded by killing D14b.\\n    31\\t- EVIDENCE: 5 FILE resources — `TASK-260830-2ciy0s_secprim-rev3.md` (31/31 AC rows with call sites, 22/29 rules narrowing-covered, R12 double probe, Windows escape-capable set + AF_UNIX/DEDUP counterexamples), battery py + log (59 killed/61 applied; N7 survives w/ bound), full-test + race logs.\\n    32\\t- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (20 pkgs), `-cover` exit 0 (secprim 94.4%), `-race` secprim+cliresult exit 0, `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet/build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0. Tree OID `7cae2bfa` identical across battery, plants, probes, finish.\\n    33\\t- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t### 1553 — Shared-environment boundary round-2 rework: admit hole closed by delegation, shape census, 27-mutant battery\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8248,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2062,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
