equireSkipArmRecordsVerdict`/`TestRequireFailArmRecordsVerdict` drive the real `Require` through both arms with a recording fake (M04/M05 killed); `TestMain` prints counters after the parallel tests. Round-2's two untrue sentences superseded in the round-3 outcome doc.\n+- C2: 2035 entry corrected in place (false counts withdrawn, digest kept, correction note added); worktree sweep clean.\n+- SURVIVORS CLOSED: M02 (empty-ID with probe), M08 (symlink strictness pinned exactly), M16 (empty operation ID), M27 (whitespace-quote message pin) — all killed. Battery re-derived from this tree: 38 applied / 0 NOT_APPLIED / 0 COMPILE_FAIL / 0 VET_FAIL, 36 killed (narrowing 26 + arm-deletion 6 + census-only 4), 2 survived with bounds: N-DriveRedactNoDelegate (N16 delegation bound) and S1-ModeBitsFalse (survive-as-SKIP). Token-preserving mutant ran the full suite. Manifest `c6018721…` identical after the battery.\n+- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest-round3.md` (6/6 AC rows, 38-row mutant table, gates with exit codes) + `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_mutant-battery-round3.log` + full-test log.\n+- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (21 pkgs), secconftest `-race` exit 0, `./... -cover` exit 0 (secconftest 92.6%, secprim 94.4%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet/build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (94 cases, unchanged), 8/8 fuzz `-fuzztime=100x` exit 0 with no corpus written, verbose 246 PASS / 0 SKIP / 0 FAIL, digest `5569f34caab734eb`.\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\n+\n+### 2105 — secconftest round-2 rework: C1–C4 closed, instrument stops reporting untrue things\n"}}}
