{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d2bf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a077c8-d88a-7931-843c-3e9dddbe9444"},"sequence":1978,"recorded_at":1780531400003951,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d502244e-0589-4672-9c20-02af4f4b0b68","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"d502244e-0589-4672-9c20-02af4f4b0b68","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d502244e-0589-4672-9c20-02af4f4b0b68"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Round 3 is handed off to review (`to-review`, checklist 18/18).\n\nWhat changed in `internal/secconftest`, all driven through the public API:\n\n- **C1 rule decided and enforced**: a crashed commit counts as committed. The commit-apply fault fires after the durable write, so the fault path stores a `recoverable_parked_state` receipt and marks finalized; `Rollback` then refuses with `ErrRollbackPastFinalize` and the bytes survive. Covered by `TestTransactorCrashedCommitIsFinal`.\n- **C1b neighbours closed as a class**: rollback-twice, commit-twice, commit-after-rollback, and prepare-after-commit are all refused with named errors (`without prepare`, `ErrCommitPastFinalize`, `ErrPreparePastFinalize`, `without staged`); prepare-after-rollback restages the recovery retry. Six subtests in `TestTransactorTerminalNeighbours`. No path inherits raw ENOENT.\n- **P7, M02, M08, M16, M27 killed**: rollback-enter armed through the Transactor; empty-ID-with-probe, exact symlink/fifo strictness, empty operation ID, and whitespace-quote message pins added.\n- **C2b wiring fixed**: `Require` takes a minimal testing handle; fake-driven tests pin both `recordVerdict` arms (M04/M05 die); `TestMain` prints counters after the parallel tests. The two untrue round-2 sentences are superseded in the new outcome doc.\n- **C2 corrected**: round-1 LOGBOOK numbers withdrawn in place (digest kept, correction note added); worktree sweep clean.\n\nEvidence (attached with task-scoped names): `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest-round3.md` (6/6 AC rows, 38-row mutant table), `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_mutant-battery-round3.log` (38 applied / 0 NOT_APPLIED / 0 COMPILE_FAIL / 0 VET_FAIL, 36 killed, 2 bounded survivors N16 + S1; token-preserving mutant ran the full suite; manifest `c6018721…` identical after), `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_full-test-round3.log` (`go test ./...` exit 0, 21 pkgs). Also green: secconftest `-race`, `go vet` + Windows vet/build, gofmt, `tracecheck` (94 cases), 8/8 fuzz `100x`, 246 PASS / 0 SKIP / 0 FAIL, digest `5569f34caab734eb`. Work left uncommitted in the worktree for the handoff snapshot.","reason":null}}
